    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Find the value of\n$$\\cos^2(1^\\circ)+\\cos^2(2^\\circ)+\\cos^2(3^\\circ)+\\cdots+\\cos^2(89^\\circ).$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$44.5$.\n\nEach of the 44 complementary-angle pairs sums to 1; the remaining $\\cos^2(45^\\circ)=\\tfrac12$.",
      "worked": "Let $S=\\sum_{k=1}^{89}\\cos^2(k^\\circ)$. Pair $k^\\circ$ with $(90-k)^\\circ$ for $k=1,\\ldots,44$. Since $\\cos(90^\\circ-k^\\circ)=\\sin(k^\\circ)$, each pair sums to 1. The unpaired term is $\\cos^2(45^\\circ)=\\tfrac12$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\nS&=\\sum_{k=1}^{44}\\left[\\cos^2(k^\\circ)+\\cos^2((90-k)^\\circ)\\right]+\\cos^2(45^\\circ)\\\\\nS&=44+\\frac12\\\\\nS&=\\frac{89}{2}\\\\\nS&=44.5.\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 56
  },
